<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    
    <h3>Can I hear the Morse code audio on my mobile phone?</h3>
    <p>Yes the audio feature works perfectly on almost all modern smartphones. When you press the play audio button our script utilizes your browsers native sound synthesizer to generate crisp telegraph beeps. Make sure your physical phone ringer switch is turned on and your media volume is comfortably raised otherwise you might not hear the playback.</p>
    
    <h3>Why is my translated text showing up as unknown hash marks?</h3>
    <p>If you see unusual hash tags appearing in your decoded results it usually means you entered a special character that does not exist in standard Morse. The original telegraph system only supported basic letters numbers and a handful of extreme essential punctuation marks. Emojis complex grammatical symbols and foreign language accents will not translate cleanly.</p>
    
    <h3>Do you need spaces between every single dot and dash?</h3>
    <p>No you do not place spaces between the dots and dashes of a single letter. You only place spaces between entirely different letters. If you do not include spaces the computer cannot determine where one letter finishes and the next letter starts which will entirely break the translation.</p>
</section>

